                <pb facs="d321-03" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve05p1/d321-03"/>

                <head>322. Memorandum From the Deputy Secretary of Defense (Packard) to the
                    Chairman, Joint Chiefs of Staff (Moorer)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d322-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d322-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1971-07-22"
                        >July 22, 1971</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d322-01" n="1" xml:id="d322-01"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>Kagnew Station Communications Facilities</item>
                </list>
                <p>I am forwarding to, the Chairman, NSC Under Secretaries Committee, the
                    conclusions of the study conducted by the JCS on the communications facilities
                    at Kagnew Station Asmara, Ethiopia.</p>
                <p>I believe that we should continue to seek ways that might allow us to phase-down
                    our facilities there whenever feasible. Therefore, I would like you to maintain
                    a continuous review of our communications requirements and submit to me any
                    changes in our need for the Kagnew facilities. Also, as requested in my
                    memorandum of 17 July 1969, the Contingency Relocation Plan for the Kagnew
                    Station Complex should be updated as required.</p>
                <p>Since our own review is partly dependent upon the telecommunications requirements
                    of the [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] located there, I
                    have suggested to the Under Secretary that it would be desirable if the [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] would also review
                    periodically its requirements.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> David Packard </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
